      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i run a small online stationery shop based in lyon and i'm trying to get my paperwork in order for an upcoming audit. can u give me a quick summary of what the main gdpr principles are for a small retailer? mainly interested in how i should be handling customer email addresses and shipping info. thanks.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "As a small online retailer in Lyon, you'll need to comply with the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) when handling customer data. Key principles to focus on are: \n\n- Collecting only necessary data (letters a and c of article 5.1) \n- Processing personal data lawfully (letter a of article 6)\n- Keeping data secure and up-to-date (article 32)\n- Informing and seeking consent from customers for data collection (for example, in your website's terms and conditions)\n\nFor handling customer email addresses, you should:\n\n- Ensure they provide a valid opt-in method using clear language (Retreat method for opt-out, Article 7 4-9)\n- Specify the data you'll be collecting and what it'll be used for\n- Keep records of opt-ins and access for auditing purposes\n\nFor shipping info, you may not need to handle it, but some may be necessary (if you're cooperating with postal services).",
