      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To keep data secure, you must implement measures to protect against \"unlawful access, unintentional destruction, accidental loss or alteration\" as stated in article 32(1)(a) of GDPR.\n\nIn practice, this means:\n\n- Implementing technical and organizational controls (e.g., encryption, SSL/HTTPS)\n- Training staff on data handling and security procedures\n- Conducting regular data security audits, backups, and incident response\n\nIt's particularly important to address 'incident response' (article 32(3) GDPR) in case you experience a breach. This includes having a plan in place to immediately stop and mitigate any breaches and notify the relevant regulatory authorities if the breach involves sensitive data.",
