      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To identify potential \"hidden\" or sneaky issues, follow a regular auditing process, focusing on:\n\n- Data handling procedures: Double-check workflows and confirm data is being stored and processed correctly\n- Access rights: Verify users' roles and permissions to ensure only authorized staff can access sensitive areas\n- Regular backups: Schedule backups frequently to ensure problem-free recovery\n\nYou can also utilize tools like data mapping and flowcharts to visualize the decision-making processes behind your data, which can help identify fragile joints or blind spots that might lead to serious data exposure.\n\nAdditionally, having a Quality Compliance Officer or certified auditor will also help testing data always against various testing criteria",
      "source": "target",
